IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

§ `SEC Regulation Crowdfunding — 17 CFR Part 227`

-- Required by the rule-version axis: an unpinned `RULES EFFECTIVE DATE` read
-- resolves to the localized current day, and localization needs a timezone.
-- The SEC's clock: Reg CF effective dates are Washington, D.C. dates.
TIMEZONE IS "America/New_York"

-- ===========================================================================
-- REGULATION CROWDFUNDING (17 CFR Part 227), as in force on 2026-07-23.
--
-- SCOPE. This module deliberately mirrors ONE external artifact: the Lexipedia
-- wiki page `reg_cf_exemptions`, which presents Reg CF as eight numbered
-- requirement groups. Those eight groups, and only those eight, are encoded
-- here, in their order:
--
--   1. Issuer eligibility            -> Rule 100(b)          (17 CFR 227.100(b))
--   2. Offering limit                -> Rule 100(a)(1)       (17 CFR 227.100(a)(1))
--   3. Investor investment limits    -> Rule 100(a)(2)       (17 CFR 227.100(a)(2))
--   4. Disclosure requirements       -> Rules 201, 201(t), 203(a)
--   5. Intermediary obligations      -> Rules 100(a)(3), 301-303
--   6. Advertising restrictions      -> Rule 204             (17 CFR 227.204)
--   7. Ongoing reporting             -> Rules 202, 203(b)
--   8. Resale restrictions           -> Rule 501             (17 CFR 227.501)
--
-- This is NOT a full formalisation of Part 227. Subpart C's funding-portal
-- registration regime (Rules 400-404), the bad-actor disqualification detail
-- (Rule 503), and the Rule 201 disclosure itemisation beyond the financial
-- statement tiers are represented only to the depth the mirrored page reaches.
--
-- SOURCES. Every rule text quoted inline is verbatim from the eCFR rendering of
-- Title 17 Part 227 at the 2026-07-23 issue date
-- (https://www.ecfr.gov/current/title-17/chapter-II/part-227), cross-checked
-- against the amending releases in the Federal Register. Nothing here was taken
-- from the mirrored wiki page; where the two disagree, the CFR governs and the
-- divergence is itemised in README.md.
--
-- THRESHOLDS AND THEIR CLOCKS. Every dollar figure is bound ONCE, as a named
-- constant in the section below, with one arm per amendment regime, newest
-- first, so every constant answers under `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` for
-- any rule date back to commencement. Four dates matter:
--
--   2016-05-16  Commencement. Release 33-9974, 80 FR 71388 (Nov. 16, 2015),
--               Part 227 text at 71537, instr. 4: "Effective May 16, 2016,
--               part 227 is revised to read as follows". Rule dates below
--               this are a curated refusal, not an answer (CORPUS-TRACK R2).
--   2017-04-12  Release 33-10332, "Inflation Adjustments ... Titles I and III
--               of the JOBS Act", 82 FR 17545 (Apr. 12, 2017), instrs. 5-6.
--               Moved every Reg CF dollar figure then in existence.
--   2021-03-15  Release 33-10884, "Facilitating Capital Formation and Expanding
--               Investment Opportunities by Improving Access to Capital in
--               Private Markets", 86 FR 3496 (Jan. 14, 2021). Raised the
--               offering limit AND changed the SHAPE of the investor limit:
--               "lesser of" -> "greater of", plus a new accredited-investor
--               carve-out. See the note at `investment limit` below.
--   2022-09-20  Release 33-11098, "Inflation Adjustments Under Titles I and III
--               of the JOBS Act", 87 FR 57394 (Sept. 20, 2022). Adjusted every
--               remaining Reg CF dollar figure. The offering limit was
--               deliberately NOT adjusted: the Commission considered $5,000,000
--               to "more than account for inflation" (87 FR at 57397).
--
-- The COVID-19 temporary rules (Rule 201(z)/(bb), 2020-05-04 through
-- 2022-08-28) are deliberately NOT modelled; inside that window and the
-- affected band, `financial statements required` refuses rather than
-- guesses. See the note at that function, and README §5.
--
-- MODELLING NOTE. Constitutive material (eligibility, limits, tiers) is encoded
-- as `DECIDE`/`MEANS` predicates carrying the CFR's own words in the FIELD
-- NAMES, with the paragraph's label riding beside its node as a truncated inert
-- string: `"(1)" ... transfer's `to the issuer of the securities``.
--
-- Under the enumeration-label ruling (2026-08-03) an inert string that merely
-- restates the node beside it is deleted -- inert never shadows active -- so a
-- verbatim quotation survives ONLY where no active node carries its words:
-- the four chapeaux that introduce a list, Rule 204(b)(1)-(3) (the closed
-- permitted-content list that `includes information beyond that permitted by
-- paragraph (b)` names only by cross-reference), and Rule 204(e) (a definition
-- whose node is literally TRUE). The `@ref` above each rule carries the
-- citation; the field name carries the words; the label carries the paragraph.
--
-- The obligation tail (Forms C-U / C-AR / C-TR, the advertising prohibition,
-- the resale restriction) is encoded as regulative rules.
-- ===========================================================================

§§ `Parties and acts`

DECLARE Actor IS ONE OF
    Issuer
    Intermediary
    Investor
    Purchaser

DECLARE Action IS ONE OF
    `file a Form C offering statement`
    `file a Form C-U progress update`
    `file a Form C-AR annual report`
    `file a Form C-TR termination of reporting`
    `advertise the terms of the offering`
    `transmit funds to the issuer`
    `transfer the securities`

§§ `Thresholds — every dollar figure, bound once, dated per regime`

-- THE RULE-VERSION AXIS. Each amended figure below carries one arm per
-- regime, newest first, selected on `RULES EFFECTIVE DATE` — so the whole
-- module answers under `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` for any rule date
-- back to commencement. Temporal closure (CORPUS-TRACK.md §2.4 trap 5):
-- every constant in the transitive read set of every dateable function is
-- dated over the same window; dating a proper subset would answer
-- confidently and wrongly inside the window.

@ref 80 FR 71388 (Rel. 33-9974), Part 227 text at 71537, instr. 4 — commencement
GIVETH A DATE
`Reg CF commenced` MEANS Date 16 5 2016

@ref 82 FR 17545 (Rel. 33-10332), instrs. 5-6 — inflation adjustment eff. 2017-04-12
GIVETH A DATE
`the 2017 inflation adjustment` MEANS Date 12 4 2017

@ref 86 FR 3496 (Rel. 33-10884), instr. 3 — the 2020 amendments, eff. 2021-03-15
GIVETH A DATE
`the 2021 amendments` MEANS Date 15 3 2021

@ref 87 FR 57394 (Rel. 33-11098), instrs. 2-3 — inflation adjustment eff. 2022-09-20
GIVETH A DATE
`the 2022 inflation adjustment` MEANS Date 20 9 2022

GIVEN amendment IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the rules in force include` amendment MEANS
    `RULES EFFECTIVE DATE` AT LEAST amendment

-- Ruling R2 (CORPUS-TRACK §8): below commencement there is no Reg CF to
-- answer for, so a rule date before 2016-05-16 is a curated refusal, not an
-- answer. ASSUME makes this a deliberate bottom: an arm that reaches it
-- stops evaluation with "... is an assumed term", naming this binding.
-- Phase 2's generated "not in force on <day>" arm is the designed
-- replacement (TEMPORAL-RULE-VERSION-DESIGN.md item 3); delete this when it
-- lands. This is not the deprecated module-parameter ASSUME style
-- (CORPUS-TRACK §1.3): no input is ever routed through it.
ASSUME `no Regulation Crowdfunding figure exists before commencement on 2016-05-16` IS A NUMBER

-- $1,000,000 as adopted (80 FR 71537); $1,070,000 from 2017-04-12
-- (82 FR 17545 instr. 5.a); $5,000,000 from 2021-03-15 (86 FR 3496 instr. 3).
-- Left deliberately unadjusted by the 2022 inflation release (87 FR at 57397).
@ref 17 CFR 227.100(a)(1) — offering maximum — https://www.ecfr.gov/current/title-17/section-227.100
GIVETH A NUMBER
`offering maximum in a 12-month period` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `the rules in force include` `the 2021 amendments`           THEN 5000000
           IF ^                            `the 2017 inflation adjustment` THEN 1070000
           IF ^                            `Reg CF commenced`              THEN 1000000
           OTHERWISE `no Regulation Crowdfunding figure exists before commencement on 2016-05-16`

-- $100,000 as adopted; $107,000 from 2017-04-12 (82 FR 17545 instr. 5.b-c);
-- $124,000 from 2022-09-20 (87 FR 57394 at 57398, instr. 2). Note: the 2022
-- release moved this figure by instr. 2.a and the Rule 201(t)(1) tier ceiling
