@ref 17 CFR 227.100(a)(2)(i)-(ii) — income/net-worth cut point — https://www.federalregister.gov/d/2022-19867
GIVETH A NUMBER
`income or net worth cut point` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `the rules in force include` `the 2022 inflation adjustment` THEN 124000
           IF ^                            `the 2017 inflation adjustment` THEN 107000
           IF ^                            `Reg CF commenced`              THEN 100000
           OTHERWISE `no Regulation Crowdfunding figure exists before commencement on 2016-05-16`

-- $2,000 as adopted; $2,200 from 2017-04-12; $2,500 from 2022-09-20.
@ref 17 CFR 227.100(a)(2)(i) — investment floor
GIVETH A NUMBER
`minimum permitted investment` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `the rules in force include` `the 2022 inflation adjustment` THEN 2500
           IF ^                            `the 2017 inflation adjustment` THEN 2200
           IF ^                            `Reg CF commenced`              THEN 2000
           OTHERWISE `no Regulation Crowdfunding figure exists before commencement on 2016-05-16`

-- $100,000 as adopted; $107,000 from 2017-04-12; $124,000 from 2022-09-20
-- (87 FR 57398 instr. 2.b, "removing the two references to $107,000").
@ref 17 CFR 227.100(a)(2)(ii) — per-investor cap
GIVETH A NUMBER
`maximum amount sold to any one investor in a 12-month period` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `the rules in force include` `the 2022 inflation adjustment` THEN 124000
           IF ^                            `the 2017 inflation adjustment` THEN 107000
           IF ^                            `Reg CF commenced`              THEN 100000
           OTHERWISE `no Regulation Crowdfunding figure exists before commencement on 2016-05-16`

-- $100,000 as adopted; $107,000 from 2017-04-12 (82 FR 17545 instr. 6.a);
-- $124,000 from 2022-09-20 (87 FR 57398 instr. 3.a).
